        <item>
            <title>1.5.5</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 10 Jul 2026 07:18:46 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>37</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Double-clicking the system links `var`, `tmp`, and `etc` (on Macintosh HD)</b> now navigates inside Explorer instead of opening Finder.<b> These root-level</b> items are system symbolic links; a quirk in how their targets were resolved made them look like plain files, so activating them handed the folder to Finder. They now resolve correctly and open in place as folder links (into `/private/…`), like any other folder.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
